(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #109. On 0.4.14, `Free` on a function-local list emitted
 `HEAP_FREE rdi` and left the slot pointing at the now-unmapped block, so
 the next length/print/append segfaulted (rc 139) - master-reproduced with
 `local_list_free.vox`. Fixed: the slot now points at the shared
 `_released_list_header` after the free, exactly like a buffer.)

To 'try it'.
    a list called 'the local numbers' is [1, 2, 3].
    Free 'the local numbers'.
    print "freed".
    print 'the local numbers''s length.
    print 'the local numbers''s empty.
    print 'the local numbers'.
    append 9 to 'the local numbers'.
    On error print "append refused".
    print 'the local numbers'.

'try it'.
print "back at top".
